From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: bound Cliffs codec caps and retain Q16 frame rates

Intersect the exact Uke OS3.0.304.0 Cliffs codec XML limits with the
same-SoC OnePlus 1138e00f instance tables. Both OEM XML variants hash to
748f378bb70638e464023767ec2bb5f9c113b38bb586f46f5ecda3dc2894160f.
Select encoder/decoder and codec limits without cloning HFI tables.
Apply profile/level/bitrate bounds before control publication and retain
the explicit Main10-encode implementation gate.

Use the encoder's physical platform pipe count rather than its absent
PIPE firmware capability in the shared clock estimate. Keep decoder
routing behavior, with a maximum-rate fallback for invalid zero pipes.

Preserve fractional rates as Q16 from S_PARM through G_PARM and both HFI
packet writers. Round up only clock estimates, compare exact Q16 rate
budgets with 64-bit arithmetic, and restore previous settings on failure.
Use per-codec frame interval budgets, reject oversize frames and round
maximum enumerated FPS down. This is source/host evidence, not target
codec or sustained-performance acceptance.

